  <h3>How do grids work in css?</h3>
  <p>
    Its mainly grid-template-rows and grid-template-columns for settings how the
    cels are arranged on the page. Then you must use grid-row and grid-column to
    set which elements are going in which cells. And use grid-template-areas if
    you want to name elements and fill those areas. grid-area takes in 4 values,
    row-start, column-start, row-end, column-end. To make an element use its
    next cel too use span but then will get overwritten by manuallu setting the
    locations. You can also use -1 in grid-template-columns or
    grid-template-rows to get to the end of the cells.
  </p>
